<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gwansan Fortress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/554">554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gwansan Fortress was fought in 554 near present-day Okcheon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> between Silla and an army of Baekje and its Gaya allies. Baekje had attacked to avenge Silla's seizure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> valley, but King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seong-of-baekje">Seong of Baekje</a> was ambushed and killed and his army destroyed. The victory secured Silla's hold on the Han basin and its access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-sea">Yellow Sea</a>.</p></div>
